  "method": "This is a continuous geometric area relaxation, not a pose search. Keep each original33-part core fixed, but ignore positive clearance and every mutual small-part constraint. Cover every allowed bracket/insert orientation/reflection, including all four insert quarter turns. The translation domain expands original stock bounds by0.001mm. Original filled-outline zero-clearance Minkowski forbidden regions are computed from exactly covering convex pieces. Shrink their union by0.001mm and intersect it with the unshrunk union, so excluded geometry stays inside the zero-clearance forbidden set. Every placement meeting the original0.2mm clearance is therefore admitted by this more permissive translation region, subject to numerical checks. For every intersecting50mm grid cell, take the convex hull of the clipped translation region and expand it by a0.001mm square; their union must cover the whole region, including any boundary line or point. Minkowski-sum each convex outer cover with every exactly covering convex moving-part piece. Union these sums, then intersect with an expanded usable stock region after removing only a shrunken subset of fixed occupied geometry. This is an outer cover of every point any individual admissible small part could occupy. Union all orientations by family and both families by sheet; sum sheet areas. Non-overlapping full inventory must fit inside these occupied-point unions, so insufficient combined or family area can reject only the recorded fixed core. Sufficient area proves no packing.",
  "numerical_scope": "Geometry uses floating original vertices. Preserve every raw obstacle, shrunken exclusion, translation region, grid hull and occupied cover. Independently verify the construction, source geometry and all known compatible placements before any conditional negative conclusion; no unrestricted impossibility or H5 claim. Negative buffers only remove forbidden material and enlarge the relaxation; they never certify an accepted placement. Stock padding and zero clearance are relaxation parameters, not changes to original acceptance.",
